   "html": "<p>A curated group of 25 influencers from Reddit sleuths to TikTok theorists received weekly cryptic clues, each one teasing a key moment from the upcoming episode. These in-world hints were intentionally vague, designed to challenge even the most devoted fans.</p>\n<p>As creators raced to decode and share their interpretations, the weekly drops sparked social speculation and amplified anticipation, turning each Tuesday into a mini fan event. This strategy sustained buzz throughout the season, helping boost viewership, drive weekly conversation, and deepen fan connection to the Daredevil universe.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "MAILER CONTENTS",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text2",
     "left": "<p>The mailer experience kicked off with an ominous newspaper clipping asking, “Where is Daredevil?” giving fans an early glimpse into the season. In week two, The Punisher made his presence known through a realistic crime scene evidence bag with hidden clues scrawled across the packaging hinting at the chaos to come. Week three amped up the action with subtle yet sinister clues tied to an upcoming bank heist. The following week shifted gears into visual storytelling, delivering an exclusive piece of David Mack artwork linked to the Muse Killer storyline. </p>",
     "right": "<p>Week five raised the stakes with formal invites to Mayor Fisk’s exclusive Black and White Ball, paired with a bullseye-inspired photographic print. The final mailer ominously cast Kingpin’s shadow over the finale, tying together all the looming threads. To build anticipation and a sense of continuity, each drop arrived in the same distinctive red packaging. This consistent presentation helped drive weekly recognition, sustain buzz, and deepen fan engagement throughout the campaign.</p>"
    },
